(Deliberately includes an 'x', which is a valid letter overall but
invalid specifically for base32 (digits only go up to 'v') - should
truncate at the 'x', parsing only "v0")
A text called s32 is "v0x1".
Set n11 to s32 as a base32 number.
Print n11.

A text called s36 is "z9a".
Set n12 to s36 as a base36 number.
Print n12.

(First character invalid for the given base -> parses as empty -> 0)
A text called s5 is "abc".
Set n13 to s5 as a base5 number.
Print n13.
